course: dictionary
lesson: 13201
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. To find the right one, look at the words and sentences around it, which are its context. «The function of the heart is to pump blood.» Here function means the job or purpose of something: the heart's job is pumping blood.
explain: «The new washing machine will function well for years.» Here function is a verb, and it means to work properly. Try your meaning in the sentence: the machine will work properly for years. It fits, so that is the meaning.
explain: «The head teacher invited parents to the school function on Friday evening.» Here a function is a formal party or event. In maths, a function is a rule that turns each input number into exactly one output number. The topic and the other words in the sentence tell you which meaning to use.
fact: A word can have more than one meaning, so check the clues around it.
fact: As a noun, «function» can mean the job or purpose of something, such as the function of the heart, which is to pump blood.
fact: As a verb, «function» means to work or operate properly.
fact: A function in maths is a rule: input 3, rule ×2 + 1, output 7.
fact: Phrases to know: function machine, function as, and a school function, which is a formal party or event.
exercise: «The function of the heart is to pump blood.» What does function mean here? | A formal party | To stop working suddenly | A very heavy load | *The job or purpose of something
exercise: A function machine has the rule ×2 + 1. If the input is 3, what is the output? | *7 | 5 | 6 | 9
exercise: «The school function starts at six o'clock, so wear your best clothes.» What is a school function? | A broken machine | A type of maths sum | A lesson about plants | *A formal party or event
test: «The new washing machine will function well for years.» What does function mean? | A job for a person | A rule for turning numbers into numbers | A party for friends | *To work properly
test: In English, what is the function of an adjective in a sentence? | *To describe a noun | To count numbers | To run a machine | To pump blood
exam: Ella says: «A function is a rule that takes each input number and gives exactly one output.» What is a function, in this sentence? | A machine that has stopped working | A short poem about numbers | *A rule that turns each input number into exactly one output number | A party with food and music
